<DocsLayout title="Multi-Agent" description="Coordinate multiple AI agents with handoffs, shared sessions, and role-based access.">
  <h1>Multi-Agent</h1>
  <p>lean-ctx supports scenarios where multiple AI agents work on the same codebase — sequentially (handoffs) or concurrently (shared sessions).</p>

  <h2>Agent Handoffs</h2>
  <p>Transfer context from one agent to another without losing state:</p>
  <pre><code>ctx_agent(action="handoff", target="agent-2", context="full")
# Transfers: session state, active task, file refs, decisions</code></pre>
  <p>The receiving agent gets a structured summary of what was done, what's pending, and all relevant context — in compressed form.</p>

  <h2>Session Sync</h2>
  <p>Multiple agents can read from the same session state:</p>
  <pre><code>ctx_agent(action="sync")  # Pull latest session state from shared storage</code></pre>

  <h2>Agent Diary</h2>
  <p>Each agent can record categorized observations for other agents:</p>
  <pre><code>ctx_agent(action="diary", category="discovery", value="Found auth bug in middleware")
ctx_agent(action="diary", category="decision", value="Using JWT over sessions")
ctx_agent(action="diary", category="blocker", value="Need DB migration first")</code></pre>
  <p>Categories: <code>discovery</code>, <code>decision</code>, <code>blocker</code>, <code>progress</code>, <code>insight</code></p>

  <h2>Role-Based Access</h2>
  <p>Assign different roles to different agents to control what each can do. See <a href="/docs/governance/">Governance</a> for role details.</p>
  <pre><code># Agent 1: Full coder access
ctx_session(action="role", value="coder")

# Agent 2: Review only
ctx_session(action="role", value="reviewer")</code></pre>

  <h2>Shared Knowledge</h2>
  <p>Project knowledge (<code>ctx_knowledge</code>) is shared across all agents automatically. Decisions and facts recorded by one agent are available to all others in the same project.</p>
</DocsLayout>
